  "notes": "Summary strip (opening balance, money in, money out, closing balance) is four boxed label/value pairs, not a table: Opening balance £2,418.36; Money in £3,697.36; Money out £2,691.64; Closing balance £3,424.08.  Letterhead (credit-union name and address, page 1 only, with a plain green disc as a logo), the running header from page 2 (statement period left, account number right) and the footer (member-services line left, \"Page n of N\" right) are furniture. The member address block (left) and the statement-details panel (right) sit side by side and read box by box; the details panel is a key/value table with no header. The transactions table is one zebra-striped table that runs across pages; Chrome repeats its header row at the top of each continuation page, and the expected table gives the header once. Several description cells have two lines (payee and reference), joined by a space. Empty money cells are empty strings. The bullet list is drawn by CSS (square markers)."
